  "description": "Three-channel Pt-100 indicator and converter (special version: range to 400 degrees C, 2 mA excitation) with three retransmission outputs and one alarm relay, with Modbus RTU",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-11-13",
  "source": "Presys, DMY-2015 / TY-2095 RTD special version sheet EE1229-00 (28 February 2007)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Indicador digital multi-ponto DMY-2015 / conversor multi-ponto TY-2095, versao especial 3 entradas RTD",
      "version": "EE1229-00",
      "date": "2007-02-28",
      "url": "https://presys.com.br/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/multiponto-aquisitor-009-02-07-ee-1229-00.pdf",
      "note": "register and coil tables, linked in issue #393"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Special version with three Pt-100 inputs (range up to 400 degrees C, excitation about 2 mA), three optional retransmission outputs (1-5 V, 0-10 V or 4-20 mA, set by jumpers) and one alarm relay (relay 4) that can work as a trip alarm. The sheet says its information takes priority over the instrument's technical manual.",
    "The document numbers registers and coils from 00 and does not say whether they are the addresses sent on the wire; they are taken as wire addresses (address_base 0). If a read is off by one, try address_base 1.",
    "The document does not give the serial settings. The slave address (0 to 99), baud rate (300 to 9600 bps) and parity are registers; 9600 bps, no parity and slave 1 are placeholders.",
    "Values shown with a decimal point on the display are sent without it. Process variables, setpoints and hysteresis values depend on the decimals of their channel and are given raw. The digital filter constant (one decimal) is scaled; percent values are given raw.",
    "The document does not say which Modbus function reads the registers; they are taken as holding registers. Registers and coils not listed are not mapped.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
